From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:41:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] spi: airoha: allow dual and quad data phases in manual mode

airoha_snand_supports_op() only accepted a data phase wider than one
wire for the SPI-NAND page operations, so a SPI-NOR on the manual path
always fell back to single-wire reads. The manual FIFO already takes
the data phase at the width it is given, including the turnaround on
the phase before it, so accept 1-1-2 and 1-1-4 operations as well. The
SPI core still limits them to what the device's bus width allows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c b/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c
index 13a65ea1..ee653253 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/airoha_snfi_spi.c
@@ -817,9 +817,12 @@ static bool airoha_snand_supports_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
 	if (airoha_snand_is_page_ops(op))
 		return true;
 
+	/*
+	 * The manual FIFO takes the data phase at the width it is given, so
+	 * 1-1-2 and 1-1-4 reads work as long as the device can do them.
+	 */
 	return (!op->addr.nbytes || op->addr.buswidth == 1) &&
-	       (!op->dummy.nbytes || op->dummy.buswidth == 1) &&
-	       (!op->data.nbytes || op->data.buswidth == 1);
+	       (!op->dummy.nbytes || op->dummy.buswidth == 1);
 }
 
 static int airoha_snand_dirmap_create(struct spi_mem_dirmap_desc *desc)
